<title>UK: HORSE RACING-ECLIPSE STAKES RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-ECLIPSE STAKES RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>SANDOWN, England 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Eclipse</p>
<p>Stakes, a group one race for three-year-olds and upwards run</p>
<p>over one mile and two furlongs (2 kms) on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Pilsudki 11-2 (ridden by Mick Kinane)</p>
<p>2. Benny The Dip 6-1 (Willie Ryan)</p>
<p>3. Bosra Sham 7-4 on favourite (Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>Five ran</p>
<p>Distances: One and a quarter lengths, short head</p>
<p>Winner owned by Lord Weinstock and trained by Michael Stoute</p>
<p>in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 145,450 pounds ($245,000).</p>
</text>
